 ### Formulas
 **Reconstruction:**
-$$ \tilde{\mathbf{r}}_n^l = \sum_{k=1}^{l} \mathbf{Z}^k[\mathbf{i}_n^k], \quad l \in \{1, \dots, L\} $$
-$$ \tilde{\mathbf{r}}_n^0 = \mathbf{0} $$ [S1]
+$$ \hat{\mathbf{r}}_n^l = \sum_{k=1}^{l} \mathbf{Z}^k[\mathbf{i}_n^k], \quad l \in \{1, \dots, L\} $$
+$$ \hat{\mathbf{r}}_n^0 = \mathbf{0} $$ [S1]
 
 **Index Selection:**
-$$ \mathbf{i}_n^l = \text{argmin}_k \| \mathbf{Z}^l[k] - (\mathbf{r}_n - \tilde{\mathbf{r}}_n^{l-1}) \|_2^2 $$ [S1]
+$$ \mathbf{i}_n^l = \text{argmin}_k \| \mathbf{Z}^l[k] - (\mathbf{r}_n - \hat{\mathbf{r}}_n^{l-1}) \|_2^2 $$ [S1]
 
 **Training Objective (Rotation):**
-$$ L_r = \frac{1}{NC} \sum_{n=1}^{N} \sum_{k=1}^{L} \| \text{sg}[\mathbf{r}_n - \tilde{\mathbf{r}}_n^{k-1}] - \mathbf{Z}^k[\mathbf{i}_n^k] \|_2^2 $$
+$$ L_r = \frac{1}{NC} \sum_{n=1}^{N} \sum_{k=1}^{L} \| \text{sg}[\mathbf{r}_n - \hat{\mathbf{r}}_n^{k-1}] - \mathbf{Z}^k[\mathbf{i}_n^k] \|_2^2 $$
 Where $\text{sg}[\cdot]$ is the stop-gradient operator [S1]. The objective for scale $L_s$ is analogous [S1].
 
